 `previews/approved-concept-*.webp` are the boards it was approved from.
 
-Production refinements over the approved concept:
+The approved concept is authoritative. At 128 pt and above (and the 64 pt
+preview tier) `seal-dark.mjs` produces the archived concept's artwork
+unchanged. Symbols, shapes, colours and materials are those of
+`design/document-icon-concepts-v1/directions/seal-dark.mjs` on the archive
+branch. The only production differences are:
 
-| Area | Change |
+| Area | Difference from the concept |
 | --- | --- |
-| ZIP | Ribbon "ladder" replaced by meshing ribbon teeth, a brass slider and parting tapes |
-| RAR | Flat slanted bars replaced by a pressed three-layer block with depth, distinct from BZIP2's bands |
-| TAR.\* | Larger compressor medallion (brass bezel, compressor-hue ring); the page fold takes the compressor hue |
-| 16 / 32 pt | Brighter sheet, firmer rose rim on dark backgrounds, narrower spine, larger glyph; compressor cues on TAR.\* |
+| 16 / 32 pt only | Slightly brighter sheet and fold, firmer rose rim on dark backgrounds, narrower spine and seam, slightly larger glyph (readability; same symbols and colours) |
 | Typography | Labels are outlined from vendored Inter Display (OFL-1.1, `fonts/OFL.txt`), so there is no font dependency |
-| Unchanged | Lacquered aubergine sheet, near-black spine, champagne-brass seam, jade stud and its restrained halo, ivory labels, per-format ribbon glyphs, transparency |
+
+An earlier production pass redrew the ZIP, RAR and compressed-TAR artwork
+(a zipper with a brass slider, an oblique block, and a larger medallion with
+a compressor-tinted fold). Those changes were reverted to the approved
+artwork; do not reintroduce design changes without explicit approval.
 
 `previews/production-board.webp` shows every production icon beside the
 approved concept, in light and dark, at large and actual small sizes.
+Single-volume archives always use their format's ordinary document icon. The
+split-volume artwork (`svg/7z-volume-*`, `previews/unregistered/`) is kept
+for a future Quick Look thumbnail extension.
 
